WHAT IS CRM?

	CRM stands for Customer Relationship Management. 
	At its simplest, it is a technology used to manage all of your company's relationships and interactions with customers and potential customers.
	"Centralization": Instead of having information scattered across sticky notes, spreadsheets, and various email threads, a CRM pulls everything into one single location.
	The "360-Degree View": It provides a complete history of every customer, including who they are, what they’ve bought, and every conversation they’ve had with your support or sales teams.
	A "Shared Goal": It isn't just for sales; it's a tool that unites marketing, sales, commerce, service, and IT under one shared understanding of the customer.
